.TH APTFZ 1 "2026-11-25" "aptfz 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
aptfz \- interactive explorer for installed apt packages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aptfz
[OPTIONS]
.br
.B aptfz \-D
.I PACKAGE NOTE
.br
.B aptfz \-D
.I PACKAGE
.B \-d
.br
.B aptfz \-\-notes\-list
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aptfz
opens an
.BR fzf (1)
picker over the installed packages, with a colorized live preview pane showing
version, dependencies, recommendations, suggestions, reverse dependencies,
size, install reason and any note you attached. After you pick a package its
full preview is printed.
.PP
.B aptfz
accepts the same filter, sort and size options as
.BR aptq (1),
which see for their full description. The options listed there determine
which packages the picker shows.
.SH OPTIONS
All filter, sort and size options of
.BR aptq (1)
(\fB\-e \-d \-n \-k \-f \-a \-x \-v \-s \-\-asc \-\-desc \-t \-\-has\-note \-\-no\-note\fR).
With \fB\-t\fR,
.B aptfz
prints a sentence describing the selection followed by the total size, instead
of opening the picker.
.SS Display options
.TP
.B \-\-exact
Use exact matching in fzf (fzf's \fB\-e\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-hide\-notes
Do not show notes in the preview.
.SS Notes
Notes are free\-text reminders attached to a package name, kept in a small
JSON file independent of the package cache.
.TP
.BI \-D " PACKAGE NOTE"
Set the note for \fIPACKAGE\fR. Must be the first argument.
.TP
.BI \-D " PACKAGE " \-d
Delete the note for \fIPACKAGE\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-notes\-list
List all packages that have notes. Must be the first argument.
.SS Other
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a usage summary.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version.
.TP
.B \-\-print\-selection
Print only the chosen package name instead of its preview. Used by the shell
key bindings.
.SH SHELL KEY BINDINGS
Source one of these from your shell's startup file:
.PP
.nf
source /usr/share/aptfz/key\-bindings.bash    # bash
source /usr/share/aptfz/key\-bindings.zsh     # zsh
.fi
.PP
This binds \fBctrl\-p\fR to open the picker and insert the selected package
name at the cursor, so \fBapt remove\fR + ctrl\-p + Enter yields
\fBapt remove firefox\fR, ready to run.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.cache/aptfz/packages.json
Self\-validating package cache (override: \fBAPTFZ_CACHE_PATH\fR). Disposable.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/aptfz/notes.json
Your notes (override: \fBAPTFZ_NOTES_PATH\fR). Not removed when the package is
uninstalled. A notes file that cannot be parsed is never overwritten.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B APTFZ_CACHE_PATH, APTFZ_NOTES_PATH
Override the file locations above. Defaults follow \fBXDG_CACHE_HOME\fR and
\fBXDG_DATA_HOME\fR.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable colored output when printing the final preview.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success or when the picker is cancelled, 1 on an error (including a
missing fzf), 2 on an invalid command line.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR aptq (1),
.BR fzf (1),
.BR apt\-mark (8),
.BR dpkg\-query (1)
